AltoVesting::submitNewPendingRoot
├── when caller is not merkle root updater or owner
│   └── it should revert with MerkleRootManagerNotUpdater
├── when vesting is not updatable
│   └── it should revert with AltoVestingNotUpdatable
├── when newMerkleRoot is zero
│   └── it should revert with MerkleRootManagerInvalidInput
├── when newMerkleRoot is same as current pending root
│   └── it should revert with MerkleRootManagerAlreadyPending
└── when all conditions are met for valid submission
    ├── when caller is merkle root updater
    |    ├── it should set pendingMerkleRoot with new merkle root
    |    ├── it should set pendingMerkleRoot with new ipfs hash
    |    ├── it should set pendingMerkleRoot validFrom to current timestamp + timelock
    |    └── it should emit SubmitPendingMerkleRoot event with correct parameters
    └── when caller is owner
         ├── it should set merkle root timelock to initialTimelock
         ├── it should set pendingMerkleRoot with new merkle root
         ├── it should set pendingMerkleRoot with new ipfs hash
         ├── it should set pendingMerkleRoot validFrom to current timestamp + timelock
         └── it should emit SubmitPendingMerkleRoot event with correct parameters
